PATH RESOLUTION NOTE (no silent drift)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The generated prompt's "Output" path `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Maps/**` does
NOT match this repository. The real, build-compiled convention (project.yml compiles
`apps/apple/Sources/**`, and every sibling P7 page — ChargingList, ChargingHeatmap,
DriveDetail, BatteryCells, EnergyPage — lives under `apps/apple/Sources/Features/<Domain>/`)
is:

    apps/apple/Sources/Features/Maps/**

The page was implemented there so it actually compiles into the iOS + macOS app
targets (verified below: every MapOverview*.swift appears as a SwiftCompile unit in the
iOS-Simulator build and the macOS build). `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Maps/` is NOT a
compiled source root in project.yml; placing files there would produce dead, uncompiled
code. Faithful interpretation of the artifact's intent ("the Maps feature directory"), not
scope narrowing — identical to the sibling ChargingHeatmap / Powershare P7 resolutions.

Native route: the page is registered on the existing AppRoute `.maps` (pathSegment "maps",
group .vehicle), which is the canonical native owner of the web /live live-map screen and was
previously unregistered. No AppRoute enum change was needed.

