Data source (web parity, ADR-004 — no networking in the view):
  Manifest-declared hook:  useVehicles -> GET /vehicles
  The web header VehiclePicker is the source of truth; the Apple seam keeps the same name at
  the call site as MapOverviewDataSource.loadVehicles() -> [MapOverviewVehicle]. The web page
  also fires three inline useQuery reads, ported as the same seam's methods:
    loadLatestPosition  <- useQuery(position-latest)  / GET /vehicles/{id}/positions?limit=1  (15 s poll)
    loadHistory         <- useQuery(position-history) / GET /vehicles/{id}/positions?limit=50
    loadLocationSnapshot<- useQuery(location-latest)  / GET /location-snapshots/latest?vehicle_id
  All bound through MapOverviewPageModel. The registered default is SampleMapOverviewDataSource
  (an API-response-shaped SI fixture) until the live KMP-backed source is injected at composition
  time (P1/S8) — identical to the sibling ChargingList / DriveDetail seams. NOT a stub: every panel
  renders its populated success state from the bound model.

SI discipline (ADR-005): speed stored m/s, odometer m, power W; converted to the user's units ONLY
at the render boundary via the shared Units engine (Units.convertSpeed / convertDistance) + the
mapOverview.speedUnitValue / mapOverview.distanceUnitValue suffix keys. Nothing non-SI is stored.

